AUDIO: 'multiple heights of the same location. You can trim the clip and change how often frames are extracted and the amount of splits. With extract one frame, you can visualize the masking before running the whole pipeline. Masking.'

[02:07] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The 360 Gaussian Pro interface in the "Masking" tab, showing "Keyword SAM3" options with "person" as a text prompt.
AUDIO: 'There are three different masking features. With fisheye footage, the circle mask is needed. There are presets for common cameras, which are auto'

[02:19] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Title card "ALIGNMENT" over a street scene.
AUDIO: 'detected. Keyword masking uses SAM 3, which detects elements with keywords. With detect this frame, you can test how masking works on a single frame. Alignment.'

[02:33] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The 360 Gaussian Pro interface in the "Alignment" tab, showing matcher, overlap, and lens prior settings.
AUDIO: 'Sequential is recommended for video. If you have GPS data, use spatial. The recommended starting overlap is 17 for raw fisheye and 10 for stitched 360. The software detects the input type and'

[02:45] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The 360 Gaussian Pro interface in the "Alignment" tab, with "Masking 2/2 - done" status.
AUDIO: 'sets it automatically. Glow map is much faster, but when scanning an interior with multiple rooms, you often get better alignment without it. If the alignment is not correct, try again with glow map off. For preset quality, default is a good starting point.'

[02:58] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The 360 Gaussian Pro interface in the "Train" tab, showing options for Lickfeld Studio, Postshot, Brush, or No Train.
AUDIO: 'Training. You can add Lickfeld Studio, pose shot, or brush to the pipeline for training. No training can also be selected. Add the path to the XE file and select'

[03:12] [scene:ui]
